WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:02.730
Ensign Cryska Barchenowa, launching.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.820
So it's self-defense now.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.410
Captain Dahl! I'm one of the ones you saved.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.080
You're a hero, you saved the lives of many 
refugees. There's no reason for us to fight!

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:28.780
No... Inia's piloting the 
Terminator by herself?

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.180
Argos 3 and 4 have a long range.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.770
We'll send them to Anchorage 
base in US territory.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.140
The rest of us will stay here and gather 
information at combat grounds A207.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.140
Afterwards we'll head to B01. There, 
we'll load up on live ammunition.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.980
Okay, you take care of things here.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.730
Don't die, you guys...

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.880
Those guys are good. They 
took out 6 TSFs unarmed.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:59.420
Keep your distance. We'll slowly tear 
them apart with guided rounds. Got it?

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:00.990
Roger!

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:06.000
<b>Untainted Revenge</b>

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.430
Enemy on radar.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.430
120 seconds until they close. Damn it!

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.930
They've got guided rounds!

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.420
What?

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.060
We're sitting ducks out here! 
We'll get our asses handed to us!

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.800
The enemy's making the obvious choice.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.060
I wanted to move before they got here.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:04.240
24 enemies. 8 with guided rounds.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.450
In a melee fight in an urban area, 
we've got at least a small chance.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.060
If we leave the ground for even 
an instant we're done for.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.730
We can't shake off that many 
guided rounds in the air.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.920
Lt. Takamura.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.420
I suggest we split our forces.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.380
One group defends this area.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.740
Another heads to B01.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.620
So we sacrifice some to save the others?

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.220
Understood.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.540
I'll stay here.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.000
You all head to B01.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.820
Wait, Yuuya!

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.990
I did lots of training against other TSFs,

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.930
including how to handle 
guided rounds, in the US military.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.360
And to take full advantage of the cover here,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.740
it's best to do it alone.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:57.340
But...!

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.330
You can't handle them all by yourself!

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.440
I'll stay here too!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.480
We can't lose both Shiranuis!

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.770
Right, Yui?

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.320
I'll show you how good your...

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:14.650
No, our, Shiranui is in actual combat.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.720
So please!

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.150
White Fang 1 to all units.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.280
We'll let Argos 1 handle this.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.240
It'll be fine.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.330
It's a hell of a lot easier 
than fighting the BETA on foot.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:37.900
Follow me, and stay low!

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.090
24 enemies in total.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.430
Eight of them with guided rounds.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.810
If you want to kill me, 
you'll need twice that!

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.310
Releasing pilot safeties.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.340
Let's go, partner!

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.130
So it was you.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.170
Captain Dahl, please!

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:30.760
We need people like you to 
make our dream a reality!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.610
I don't make friends with terrorists.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:37.050
We're not terrorists.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.810
We're a voice for the voiceless!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.280
Captain Dahl, if you come with us,

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.340
nothing would give us more courage!

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.760
I'm no hero.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.760
And my rank right now is Lieutenant.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:52.900
Lieutenant?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.540
Did they demote you because of what happened?

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.540
Mariem, right?

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.600
You may be right, and there's 
something wrong with the world.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:07.640
But that doesn't give you 
the right to kill anyone.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:15.170
My mother sold her body to 
raise me and my brothers.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:19.020
She killed people, and was 
eventually killed herself.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.370
And you're telling me to allow a system 
that lets that happen to exist?

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:27.900
You know what's going on in those 
refugee camps better than anyone.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.530
Help us, please, Captain Dahl!

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.570
I don't want to kill you!

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:40.020
I once made my men die to save you refugees.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.220
S-11 is in place.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:00.010
If Eurasia is recaptured,

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:02.730
the USSR will have the world's 
largest supply of G-Elements.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.170
That can't be allowed to happen.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.220
We're withdrawing 3km.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.900
After we've confirmed the target's 
destruction we head to Yukon.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:14.040
Roger.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.130
Keep firing, damn it! Keep on firing!

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.230
How many have I taken out?

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.600
How many are left?

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.410
No!

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:56.970
What?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.940
Yuuya!

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:04.750
Inia?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:07.840
You're safe?

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.710
Yes! I was so scared, Yuuya!

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.680
Christ... Stay close to me!

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.930
No way. That Terminator...

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:25.060
We used all our guided rounds!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:29.100
Damn it! What kind of magic are they using?

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.190
This is Viper 2!

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:34.500
I've lost all my unmanned units!

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.900
Permission to withdraw!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.330
What's wrong, Viper 2? Viper 2!

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:45.280
Reinforcements! Enemy reinforcements...

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:53.280
Inia!

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.720
Cryska!

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:00.640
Yui?

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.770
Are you okay, Argos 1?

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.120
What are you doing here?

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:11.440
We found Ensign Sestina's Terminator.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:14.190
We had asked to meet up with her first.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.570
Found her...?

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.880
How, with this jamming?

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.950
We can't get into USSR territory 
without someone leading the way.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.960
That's impossible...

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:30.810
There were 24 of them! And 
we gave them guided rounds!

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.570
This is Viper 4! I'm out of ammo!

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:36.470
Repeat, I am out of ammo! Help!

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.720
All units, turn command of 
the unmanned TSFs to me.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:44.440
Withdraw and report this to the Major.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:45.640
Roger.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:49.480
I'm not like my sister.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:54.580
I'll show you the pride and stubbornness 
of someone backed into a corner!

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.620
What the heck?

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.850
They're acting differently.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:10.630
A suicide attack?

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:16.630
Yifei!

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:20.140
I'm out of ammo too!

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.600
Are you okay?

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.160
Of course I am.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.400
It was close since I was out of ammo, though.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:43.320
I'll recover their equipment.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:53.710
God, I am coming to be with you!

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.180
What?

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.570
Yifei!

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:10.660
I don't regret saving you.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.620
But when I told their 
families how my men died,

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.440
I understood something.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.540
You can't stop this tragedy 
down in the field.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:22.700
If you want to change things, 
you have to climb higher.

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:26.280
Then what of those who can't do that?

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.620
Are they just supposed to accept being 
discriminated against, and treated like garbage?

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:35.120
If we can't see how things will turn out 
either way, we just have to keep going forward!

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:35.970
Mariem.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:41.060
I wish I could show you the answer,

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.690
but I don't have it myself yet.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.740
Captain Dahl...

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:51.730
What?

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.560
I didn't want to bother 
you during the mission,

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.240
but I've got bad news.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:57.840
What is it?

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:59.730
Your sister is dead.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:04.740
She was surrounded by 
the enemy and massacred.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:07.480
I see.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.660
We need to rebuild our forces.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:14.870
I'm going to launch in a TSF, 
so I'd like you to come back.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.520
Understood. I'll be right there.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.490
My sister died.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:26.130
Your sister was here too?

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:29.410
Yes. She was a fighter in the RLF.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:30.970
So I knew it could happen.

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.130
When she was young she cried all the time.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:36.640
She was a good kid.

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:39.980
Mariem.

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:41.420
Captain...

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.070
The answer you never found...

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:47.130
I think I've found it.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.460
I'm going to take revenge for her.

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:53.330
On this horrible world...

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:56.040
Stop it, Mariem. You can't!

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.930
Damn it!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:09.640
That's enough!

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:11.860
Leave him.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.450
GF-7 to all bones.

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:26.800
We are going to attempt an airspace 
infiltration over Yukon base.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:32.290
Our observation satellites have confirmed 
that the BETA exercises are a fake.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:36.410
But there's a good chance the 
terrorists will be using SAMs.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:39.360
Everyone, stay sharp.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:43.460
Be prepared for some casualties.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:46.040
The world needs stability.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:52.370
Anyway, what do you think they're after?

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:57.810
The Yukon area is limited in the number of 
forces there because of our treaties with Russia.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:03.170
And it's an important relay station in our 
military comm network, which makes it a good target.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:04.070
I see.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:09.070
So we can't put too many forces there 
without sparking a conflict with the Russians?

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.880
But the whole thing is so clumsy.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:12.580
What do you mean?

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.900
Yukon base doesn't have any real AA weaponry.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.410
If they ignore the hostages 
and attack anyway...

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:24.500
What was that-?

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:25.500
Laser Class?

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.170
You're kidding me! This is North America!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:35.430
I've heard rumors that there's a 
US BETA research base in Alaska.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.700
Then the terrorists set the BETA free?

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:39.640
Why?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.570
That was probably a bomber 
squadron that just got shot down.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:47.690
They used the Laser Class as an AA defense.

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:53.320
So they've got the best 
anti-air system possible?

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:01.520
Cryska!

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:02.560
Inia!

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:07.610
Um... um...

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.930
I was so scared! So scared!

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.970
I'm sorry, Inia.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.350
It's okay now.

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.700
Family... huh?

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:35.560
The enhancement membrane 
is set to keep it stable.

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:40.130
But I'm amazed you managed to 
bail-out from that explosion.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:41.870
I've got good karma.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.380
You're an impressive woman.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:46.890
I can't die here.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:48.980
We haven't gone on our date yet.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:54.140
Lt. Takamura, it's Sandek.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.390
We've transferred our pilot.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:57.880
Roger.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:02.890
We've finished our first aid, but it's 
going to be difficult to move Lt. Cui.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:07.860
Don't worry about me. The 
painkillers are kicking in.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.780
I hate to say it, but you 
can take care of the rest.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:15.180
The jamming's weakened.

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:17.800
They're finally ready for 
their big message, huh?

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:25.680
We are the RLF.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:28.140
The Refugee Liberation Front.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.300
This is a message for the entire world.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:36.800
Your cruel treatment of the Eurasian 
Refugees since the start of the BETA war

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.370
will not be allowed to stand!

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:46.090
The refugee aid groups are nothing but a 
hotbed of sloth, corruption, and embezzlement.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:52.050
You are well aware that the 
refugee camps are victims of

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:57.950
violence, starvation, drug addiction, 
and forced conscription,

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:03.450
but the governments of the developed 
countries in the Americas, Africa, and Oceania,

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.960
not only refuse to take any measures 
to improve these conditions,

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:11.720
but conspire with the UN to funnel 
vast amounts of money to contractors

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.960
for the development of TSFs.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.650
These are the demands of the RLF.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:22.360
The elimination of corruption. Guarantees 
of protection for the refugees.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.850
Guaranteed elections for the countries 
whose citizens are in the camps!

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.300
We will not give in to any form of pressure.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:34.460
Just now the cowardly Americans 
sent in a team of bombers,

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:37.930
and attempted to wipe us 
out with neutron bombs.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.210
More of them? Go away already.

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:44.280
Wait!

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:45.500
This is somehing else.

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:47.740
Code 991.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.500
A BETA attack?

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:55.260
In order to protect the lives of the tens of 
thousands of civilians that remain in the base,

00:17:55.760 --> 00:18:01.000
we were forced to release the Laser Class 
from the US's top-secret BETA research facility.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.000
And we were able to stop 
them at the last second.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.160
Wait, VG!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:09.060
Our first priority is 
to make it to Anchorage!

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.770
Those were Anchorage bombers 
that got wiped out!

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:15.020
We need more information 
on those Laser Class.

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:23.700
America's criminal and murderous 
acts extend far beyond this.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:29.170
We now release to the world information 
about an even greater evil

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:32.290
that was given to us by a 
high-ranking Soviet official.

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:36.610
The North American absolute 
defense line, Red Shift.

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:42.490
This is a defense system that protects 
North America from a BETA invasion.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:47.610
In the event a certain number 
of BETA reach this line,

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:52.650
a series of hydrogen bombs placed in a line 
across Alaska will detonate simultaneously.

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:57.730
This will create an artificial strait that 
can be used to create a new defense line.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:02.720
In other words, the activation of this defense 
system means the slaughter of every Soviet citizen.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:10.290
We admit our mistake in releasing the BETA 
without knowing of this inhuman system.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.540
But the truth is unmistakable.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:17.280
You haven't much time left.

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:19.210
I hope you'll make the right decision.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:21.680
Lt. Takamura.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:25.450
You don't have time to listen 
to her ramble, do you?

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:27.660
I'm fine. Go.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:30.010
But I can't leave you here...

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:31.570
Don't worry.

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:36.090
Lt. Sandek's car shouldn't be that far off.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:38.840
I'll use it to get back 
to the Bao-Feng hangar.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:41.890
I'm not going to let myself 
slow you guys down.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.060
Take this in case you need it.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.980
Thanks.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.540
Zai jian.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:03.460
White Fang 1 to all units. Prepare to move.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.390
Is she serious? Are they 
gonna blow up Alaska?

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:10.160
Why would they do that?

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:12.700
Yui. Did you know anything about this?

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:13.770
No.

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:15.840
What about you, Lt. Sandek?

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:17.100
No.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:19.020
But it's possible.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:26.780
It would make sense if they had such a system in 
place even before they allowed us to settle in Alaska.

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:31.010
Then we need to wipe out the BETA in 
addition to stopping the terrorists.

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:34.290
And we'll have to do it ourselves.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:38.060
Most of the Soviet military 
is stationed in Kamchatka

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:41.120
or the Alaskan coast and simply 
uses the base as a relay point.

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:44.170
Even if we responded immediately 
there's limits to what we can do.

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:47.820
There's no time left to resupply at B01.

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:53.680
But we don't have the fuel or 
ammunition left to stop all of them.

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.460
Damn it. We're stuck then?

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:58.000
No, there's a way.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.940
Of course, it's risky.

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:05.320
The Soviet Patrol hangar.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:09.030
There'll be fuel and ammo there.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:14.680
Sure, but it's right in 
the middle of the enemy!

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:16.140
That's why it's a good idea.

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:20.040
They won't be expect us to 
attack in this situation.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:21.290
Are you serious?

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:22.940
I see.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.290
I overlooked that.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.420
And...

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:29.430
In a guerilla war, the best thing you 
can do is take weapons from your enemy.

00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:31.930
I'm sick of running.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:35.060
It's time to go on the offensive.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:38.480
You're wonderful, Yuuya!

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:41.320
You really are wonderful.

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:47.700
How's it going?

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:51.020
We've tuned it to match 
your personal data, Major.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:54.950
There'll still be a bit of sensory 
lag, but you can handle it.

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:58.960
And we've added that device in as well.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:02.090
You must prepare to evacuate.

00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:04.880
We're done playing terrorist.

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:06.170
Roger.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.400
Now we can be rid of those 
stupid idealists, right?

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:11.470
Yes.

00:22:21.680 --> 00:22:26.280
At last that squad of supermen will be mine!

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:09.220
They say the Eishi here 
are the best in the world!

00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:11.250
Show me what you can do!

00:24:11.250 --> 00:24:15.000
We are the one thing that 
can avert destruction.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:16.510
I'm expecting your best.

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:20.280
Hey, Cryska, what is it you want to protect?

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:24.310
<b>The Victory Song of the Dead</b>

00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:23.810
Next time on Total Eclipse: The Victory Song of the Dead.
